#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:6
msgid "Windows (binary)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:10
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:12
msgid ""
"This page explains how to install ROS 2 on Windows from a pre-built binary "
"package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:16
msgid ""
"The pre-built binary does not include all ROS 2 packages. All packages in "
"the `ROS base variant <https://reps.openrobotics.org/rep-2001/#ros-base>`_ "
"are included, and only a subset of packages in the `ROS desktop variant "
"<https://reps.openrobotics.org/rep-2001/#desktop-variants>`_ are included. "
"The exact list of packages are described by the repositories listed in `this "
"ros2.repos file <https://github.com/ros2/ros2/blob/rolling/ros2.repos>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:21
msgid "System requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:23
msgid "Only Windows 11 is supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:28
msgid "Create a location for the ROS 2 installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:30
msgid ""
"This location will contain both the installed binary packages, plus the ROS "
"2 installation itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:32
msgid ""
"Start a Command Prompt session (usually by clicking on the start menu, then "
"typing ``Command Prompt``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:34
msgid ""
"Then create a directory to store the installation. Because of Windows path-"
"length limitations, this should be as short as possible. We'll use ``C:"
"\\dev`` for the rest of these instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:38
msgid "$ md C:\\dev"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:43
msgid "Install prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:45
msgid ""
"ROS 2 uses `conda-forge <https://conda-forge.org/>`__ as a backend for "
"packages, with `pixi <https://pixi.sh/latest/>`__ as the frontend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:49
msgid ""
"The installation of conda-forge may trigger Windows Defender to treat it as "
"a threat, but this can be safely ignored by clicking \"More info\" and \"Run "
"anyway\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:52
msgid "Install pixi"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:54
msgid ""
"Use use the instructions on https://pixi.sh/latest/ to install ``pixi`` "
"either with the Windows Installer or using command line in your opened "
"Command Prompt terminal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:56
msgid ""
"Once ``pixi`` has been installed, close the Command Prompt session and start "
"it again, which will ensure ``pixi`` is on the PATH."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:60
msgid "Install ROS 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:62
msgid ""
"Binary releases of Rolling Ridley are not provided. Instead you may download "
"nightly :ref:`prerelease binaries <Prerelease_binaries>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:65
msgid ""
"Download the latest package for Windows, e.g., ``ros2-package-windows-AMD64."
"zip``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:66
msgid ""
"Unpack the zip file somewhere on your system (we'll assume ``C:\\dev\\``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:67
msgid ""
"Change the name of the extracted folder to match the distro (we'll assume "
"``C:\\dev\\rolling``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:71
msgid "Install Pixi dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:73
msgid ""
"Go to the folder where you unzipped the ROS 2 prereleased binaries and "
"install the dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:75
msgid ""
"$ cd C:\\dev\\rolling\n"
"$ pixi install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:81
msgid "Run preinstall installation script"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:83
msgid ""
"Run the preinstall installation setup script to make sure that the zipped "
"file are able to run in the current folder the ROS 2 binaries have been "
"exctrated to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:85
msgid "$ pixi run python preinstall_setup_windows.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:91
msgid "Install additional RMW implementations (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:93
msgid ""
"The default middleware that ROS 2 uses is ``Fast DDS``, but the middleware "
"(RMW) can be replaced at runtime. See the :doc:`guide <RMW-Implementations/"
"Working-with-multiple-RMW-implementations>` on how to work with multiple "
"RMWs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:97
msgid "Install Visual Studio Build Tools 2022 (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:99
msgid ""
"To compile packages written in C++, install Visual Studio Build Tools 2022. "
"During installation, select the \"Desktop development with C++\" workload to "
"ensure the MSVC compiler and Windows SDK are available. Download from `here "
"<https://visualstudio.microsoft.com/vs/older-downloads/#visual-studio-2022-"
"and-other-products>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:104
msgid ""
"Run all commands in the \"x64 Native Tools Command Prompt for VS "
"2022\" (available from the Start Menu), which configures the required build "
"environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:109
msgid "The full Visual Studio IDE is not required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:112
msgid "Setup environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:114
msgid ""
"In either the same Command Prompt terminal or a new one, you can source the "
"ROS 2 environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:117
msgid "Source the environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:119
msgid ""
"In every Command Prompt you open to setup the ROS 2 workspace, source the "
"pixi environment and the ROS2 environment:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:121
msgid ""
"$ cd C:\\dev\\rolling\n"
"$ pixi shell\n"
"$ call C:\\dev\\rolling\\local_setup.bat"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:127
msgid ""
"If you do not have RTI Connext DDS installed on your computer, it is normal "
"to receive a warning that it is missing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:130
msgid "Try some examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:132
msgid ""
"In a Command Prompt, set up the ROS 2 environment as described above and "
"then run a C++ ``talker``\\ :"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:134
msgid "$ ros2 run demo_nodes_cpp talker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:138
msgid "Start another Command Prompt terminal and run a Python ``listener``\\ :"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:140
msgid "$ ros2 run demo_nodes_py listener"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:144
msgid ""
"You should see the ``talker`` saying that it is ``Publishing`` messages and "
"the ``listener`` saying ``I heard`` those messages. This verifies both the C+"
"+ and Python APIs are working properly. Hooray!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:150
msgid "Next steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:152
msgid ""
"Continue with the tutorials to configure your environment, create your own "
"workspace and packages, and learn ROS 2 core concepts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:155
msgid "Troubleshoot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:157
msgid ""
"Troubleshooting techniques can be found :ref:`here <windows-"
"troubleshooting>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:160
msgid "Uninstall"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:162
msgid ""
"If you installed your workspace with colcon as instructed above, "
"\"uninstalling\" could be just a matter of opening a new terminal and not "
"sourcing the workspace's ``setup`` file. This way, your environment will "
"behave as though there is no Rolling install on your system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:165
msgid ""
"If you're also trying to free up space, you can delete the entire workspace "
"directory with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Windows-Install-Binary.rst:167
msgid "$ rmdir /s /q C:\\dev\\rolling"
msgstr ""
